# Session artifacts
.clavain/scratch/
.clavain/verdicts/
.clavain/quality-gates/
.clavain/reviews/
.clavain/checkpoint.json
.clavain/intercore.db
.clavain/intercore.db.backup-*

# Authz signing keys — private ONLY; pubkey is intentionally committed for verifiers.
.clavain/keys/*.key
.clavain/keys/*.archive
.clavain/**/*.db
.clavain/**/*.db-shm
.clavain/**/*.db-wal
!.clavain/keys/*.pub

# Runtime
*.db.backup-*
/ic
/ic.exe
.tldrs/
.tldrsignore

# Local tooling state that lives inside this tree.
#
# Both are created by tooling, never by a build, and neither belongs to any
# commit. Left untracked they are not harmless: `go build` derives its VCS
# stamp from `git status --porcelain`, which counts untracked paths, so every
# binary built here reported `dirty: true` and matched no commit. That is what
# rig-health's ic-provenance check had been failing on -- a deployed `ic` whose
# provenance could not be established, from a tree whose only modification was
# a beads store and a worktree directory.
#
# Sylveste's root .gitignore and the marketplace sibling already ignore these;
# intercore was the repo that never got the same treatment.
.beads/
.claude/worktrees/
